---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Projects - Steve Wang"
  description="Selected projects by Steve Wang, including digital signage CMS work, QuotaStation, StackVitals, Fuel Tracker, Shared Bill, and Ordering Dashboard."
  current="projects"
>
  <main>
    <section class="page-title section-wrap">
      <h1>Projects</h1>
      <p>
        Selected work across full-stack product development, live personal software,
        local-first desktop software, operations dashboards, and purchasing workflow automation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section-wrap project-list">
      <article class="detail-card" id="digital-signage-cms">
        <div class="detail-header">
          <div>
            <span class="project-meta">Full-stack product</span>
            <h2>Digital Signage CMS</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="status-label">Production work</span>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Scope</h3>
            <p>Production CMS for digital signage content, screens, assets, templates, editing, permissions, billing, and deployment workflows.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Owned Work</h3>
            <p>Permission control, Stripe payment setup, related CMS flows, CI/CD pipeline work, backend APIs, database changes, and production support.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Also Supported</h3>
            <p>CRM sync, screen monitoring notifications, Electron support, and Android/Tizen TV app maintenance.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Tech Stack</h3>
            <p>React, TypeScript, Node.js, MySQL, Stripe API, Ontraport CRM, Docker, Nginx, CircleCI, Bitbucket Pipelines, AWS EC2.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="detail-card" id="stackvitals">
        <div class="detail-header">
          <div>
            <span class="project-meta">Open-source dashboard</span>
            <h2>StackVitals</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="status-label">Public repo</span>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Purpose</h3>
            <p>Self-hosted dashboard for solo developers, combining uptime, deploy health, cloud cost, AI/CI usage, and domain status. A Needs Attention panel surfaces each warning with its project, provider, and error detail.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Collectors</h3>
            <p>Scheduled, opt-in adapters cover HTTP, Amplify, GitHub Actions, Cloudflare, AWS cost, Supabase health, Resend verification, and OpenAI usage. Retained snapshots power 30-day health, spend, and usage trends.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Data Safety</h3>
            <p>Collectors store aggregate signals only — never raw app records. Frontend login gates the dashboard before data renders, and Supabase RLS restricts reads to approved users.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Tech Stack</h3>
            <p>React, Vite, TypeScript, Supabase Auth with row-level security, scheduled GitHub Actions collectors, AWS Amplify Hosting, Astro Starlight project site, and Vitest with mocked provider tests.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="project-links">
          <a href="https://stackvitals.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">stackvitals.dev</a>
          <a href="https://stackvitals.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Live demo</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/SteveWang92/stackvitals" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-strip" aria-label="StackVitals screenshots">
          <figure>
            <img src="/assets/stackvitals-overview.png" alt="StackVitals overview dashboard showing deploy status, uptime, and cost for multiple projects." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Overview with per-app health and cost</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img src="/assets/stackvitals-collectors.png" alt="StackVitals collector diagnostics showing run history and provider health status." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Collector diagnostics across providers</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="detail-card" id="quotastation">
        <div class="detail-header">
          <div>
            <span class="project-meta">Private Windows app</span>
            <h2>QuotaStation</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="status-label">Private release · active development</span>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Purpose</h3>
            <p>Local-first monitoring for AI coding subscriptions, bringing live quota windows and reset times together with historical token usage, model activity, and API-equivalent cost.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Windows Surfaces</h3>
            <p>A tray quick panel, optional taskbar widget, dashboard, and Claude Code status line share one Codex and Claude Code snapshot. Alerts cover low quota, unavailable providers, and resets.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Data Safety</h3>
            <p>Reads data already published by local clients and keeps history in SQLite. Access is read-only; prompts, source code, credentials, and session content never leave the machine.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Tech Stack</h3>
            <p>Tauri 2, Rust, React, TypeScript, SQLite, Windows taskbar and notification APIs, and a provider-adapter architecture.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="detail-card" id="fuel-tracker">
        <div class="detail-header">
          <div>
            <span class="project-meta">Personal product</span>
            <h2>Fuel Tracker</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="status-label">Private release</span>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Problem</h3>
            <p>Off-the-shelf fuel apps felt heavy and missed wanted features, so refill records never stayed consistent.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Solution</h3>
            <p>Cloud web and portable Windows builds share AI-assisted logging, English/Chinese UI, and independent region, currency, and unit settings. Advisory history checks flag likely mistakes, missed fills, and unusual consumption.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>AI Extraction</h3>
            <p>Receipt photos prefill litres, pump price, fuel grade, brand, station, and purchase time across Australian and Chinese formats, with cloud token usage visible in Settings.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Tech Stack</h3>
            <p>React, TypeScript, Vite, Vitest, Electron portable build, AWS Amplify Hosting, Cognito auth, AppSync/DynamoDB data, Lambda receipt extraction.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-strip" aria-label="Fuel Tracker screenshots">
          <figure>
            <img src="/assets/fueltracker-overview.png" alt="Fuel Tracker overview showing consumption, cost, distance, and recent activity." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Overview metrics and recent activity</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img src="/assets/fueltracker-ai-entry.png" alt="Fuel Tracker add-fill screen showing AI receipt extraction filling fuel details." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>AI-assisted receipt entry</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="detail-card" id="shared-bill">
        <div class="detail-header">
          <div>
            <span class="project-meta">Personal web app</span>
            <h2>Shared Bill</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="status-label">Private release</span>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Purpose</h3>
            <p>Hosted app for recording shared expenses, splitting costs, and calculating who should pay whom.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Hosted Web App</h3>
            <p>AWS-hosted sign-in, groups with member roles and invites, weighted expense splits, settlement calculation, completed transfer tracking, and English/Chinese UI. Settlement details export as a shareable PNG image.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Import Path</h3>
            <p>Owner-only desktop JSON import keeps the original Electron data path useful while moving shared records into the hosted backend.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Tech Stack</h3>
            <p>React, Vite, TypeScript, AWS Amplify Hosting, Cognito, API Gateway, Lambda, DynamoDB, CDK, Electron, a shared settlement core, and Vitest unit/UI tests.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-strip" aria-label="Shared Bill screenshots">
          <figure>
            <img src="/assets/sharebill-expenses.png" alt="Shared Bill expenses tab with an add-expense form and a list of recorded expenses showing payer, amount, and participants." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Expense entry with participant selection</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img src="/assets/sharebill-settlement.png" alt="Shared Bill settlement tab showing a minimal transfer plan and a per-person paid, shared, and net balance table." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Settlement plan and per-person balances</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="detail-card" id="purchasing-workflow-tools">
        <div class="detail-header">
          <div>
            <span class="project-meta">Purchasing workflow app</span>
            <h2>Ordering Dashboard</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="status-label">Private release · v1.3</span>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Goal</h3>
            <p>Speed up low-stock ordering decisions that are possible in Excel but slow to prepare and check by hand.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Import &amp; Tracking</h3>
            <p>Imports checklist, stock, sales, price/cost, supplier, purchase-order, and sales-order data from Excel or ODS into local SQLite. Optional reference sheets and configurable groups support different workbook layouts.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Ordering &amp; Review</h3>
            <p>Calculates quantities from demand, stock cover, MOQ, packaging constraints, and order cycles. Buyers can adjust commitments, keep notes and rules, review trends, and safely remove backed-up imports.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Output &amp; Next Phase</h3>
            <p>Exports draft orders, supplier PDFs, and styled low-stock workbooks by buying group. Next, Weekly Report Manager will join the app so one import feeds purchasing and weekly reporting.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Tech Stack</h3>
            <p>Python, PySide6, SQLite, Pandas, OpenPyXL, Excel/ODS import, and CSV/XLSX/PDF export.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
